<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Upper Assam</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> is the eastern part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmaputra">Brahmaputra</a> valley in the Indian state of Assam, including the districts of Dibrugarh, Tinsukia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sivasagar">Sivasagar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jorhat">Jorhat</a> and Golaghat. It was the heartland of the Ahom kingdom, whose capitals stood there, and in the nineteenth century it became the centre of Assam's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">tea</a> industry and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s first oil field at Digboi.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/upper-assam.jpg" alt="Upper Assam" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dhruba Jyoti Baruah · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jorhat_Baruah_Chariali.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
